        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "510e5dcc-5f26-5907-97ac-e303a67aaed1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John Kirby, Benny Goodman\n- Music Works: \"Loch Lomond\", \"Undecided\", \"The Bonnie Banks o' Loch Lomond\"\n- Groups: John Kirby sextet\n- Genres and Topics: chamber jazz, jazz standards, Scottish song traditions\n\nFacts:\n- In the late 1930s and early 1940s, John Kirby led a successful chamber jazz sextet.\n- John Kirby also worked as a sideman, prominently with Benny Goodman.\n- John Kirby's sextet had hit songs including \"Loch Lomond\" and the debut recording of \"Undecided\".\n- \"Undecided\" became a jazz standard.\n- In Scotland, \"The Bonnie Banks o' Loch Lomond\" is often the final piece of music played during an evening of revelry, such as a dance party or dinner.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "5d899e67-2181-5062-a127-5d386ef682cc",
        "text": "Page: John Kirby (musician). Sentence: In addition to sideman work (prominently with Benny Goodman), Kirby is remembered for leading a successful chamber jazz sextet in the late 1930s and early 1940s, which scored several hit songs including \"Loch Lomond\" and the debut recording of \"Undecided\", a jazz standard.\nPage: The Bonnie Banks o' Loch Lomond. Sentence: In Scotland, the song is often the final piece of music played during an evening of revelry (a dance party or dinner, etc.).",
